INN++ generic Linux tarball
===========================

INN++ is a C++20/CMake conversion of INN 2.8.0, the InterNetNews server.
This tarball holds a prebuilt /usr/local/news for glibc Linux systems
without a native package (Debian and Ubuntu: use the .deb instead).

Requirements
------------

- glibc as new as Debian testing's at build time, and the run-time
  libraries SQLite 3, zstd and PAM (installed on most systems).
- OpenSSL is built in (nnrpd's TLS), so the system's OpenSSL updates do
  not reach it: install a newer INN++ tarball after an OpenSSL security
  release.
- Built without the Perl and Python filters, which tie the programs to
  one Perl and one Python version; build from source for those.

Install
-------

    tar -xzf inn2-cxx-<version>-linux-<arch>.tar.gz
    cd inn2-cxx-<version>-linux-<arch>
    sudo ./install.sh

install.sh creates the news group and user when absent, installs into
/usr/local/news with INN's owners (news), and makes innbind setuid root,
the only setuid-root file.  inn.conf (with this host as pathhost), the
other configuration files, active, newsgroups and the history database
are created only when absent, so running a newer install.sh upgrades the
programs and keeps the site's files.  On a systemd host the unit is
installed in /etc/systemd/system but not enabled:

    sudo systemctl enable --now inn

Then configure INN in /usr/local/news/etc; see the documents in
/usr/local/news/doc and the man pages (inn.conf(5), readers.conf(5),
incoming.conf(5), newsfeeds(5)).

Remove
------

    sudo systemctl disable --now inn; sudo rm /etc/systemd/system/inn.service
    sudo rm -rf /usr/local/news       # also removes the spool and history

Source, license and issues: https://github.com/ecarew/inn2 (LICENSE here).
